{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Task execution history for current Human Owners",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "Only GET/HEAD. Same original Project/Task/Execution membership and current Session/Owner are checked on every request, including archived projects under the original Read gate. No admin bypass. Unknown/duplicate/empty/noncanonical query fields, request bodies, Range/If-Range and Content-Encoding are rejected. One 2s handler budget; cancellation waits for the actual domain/Store/HTTP tail. Read-only business access still registers and closes its technical execution-call owner. No runtime invocation, stream, resync, cancel or Task transition. The separate runtime-view endpoint exposes only the original producer's durable final text snapshot."
  },
